---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { page, breadcrumb } from '../lib/seo';
const schema = [page('WebPage', { site:Astro.site, path:'/scope', name:'Scope and disclaimers', description:'What Ground Floor is, what it has measured, and what it cannot advise.' }), breadcrumb(Astro.site, [{name:'Scope & Disclaimers',path:'/scope'}])];
---
<Base title="Scope & Disclaimers" description="What Ground Floor is, what it has measured, and what it cannot advise." appearance="light" schema={schema}>
  <header class="gf-page-hero"><div class="gf-shell"><p class="gf-eyebrow">Scope</p><h1 class="gf-display mt-4">Ground Floor tests technical workflows. It does not replace professional judgment.</h1><p class="gf-lede">Today the site contains three validation protocols and zero completed regulated-workflow studies.</p></div></header>
  <section class="gf-content"><div class="gf-shell max-w-4xl space-y-10"><div><h2 class="gf-h2">What Ground Floor is</h2><p class="gf-copy mt-4">An independent education and field-testing project. It develops narrow, reviewable protocols for local, open-weight AI on hardware the operator controls.</p></div><div><h2 class="gf-h2">What it is not</h2><p class="gf-copy mt-4">It is not a law firm, medical provider, accounting firm, investment adviser, compliance service, security auditor, or certification body. Nothing here is legal, medical, tax, accounting, investment, compliance, or security advice.</p></div><div><h2 class="gf-h2">What “local” does not prove</h2><p class="gf-copy mt-4">On-device model inference can remove a request to a third-party model API. It does not establish that the full workflow is offline, secure, private, accurate, useful, or compliant. Access controls, storage, logs, backups, networks, review, retention, and professional rules still matter.</p></div><div><h2 class="gf-h2">How to read the evidence</h2><p class="gf-copy mt-4"><strong>Protocol</strong> means a test plan. <strong>Estimated</strong> means a disclosed calculation, not a retained run. <strong>Third-party</strong> means a named external source. <strong>Measured</strong> requires retained configuration, fixtures, raw output, timing, errors, and evaluation. No regulated workflow currently has that final label.</p><a class="gf-link inline-flex mt-5" href="/experiments">Inspect the evidence ledger →</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
